# FrontDesk Messaging UI

## Conversation Thread
- Render message bubbles with sender name, timestamp, status icons (✓ sent, ✓✓ read).
- Keep the view auto-scrolled to the latest message unless the user manually scrolls up.
- Surface typing indicators ("User is typing…") with animated feedback below the thread.
- Support rich text content (links, bold, emoji) and sanitize HTML before injecting into the DOM.

## Channel Sidebar
- Group items by channels vs. direct messages; display unread counts using `Typography` with `color="text.secondary"`.
- Show presence dots (`🟢 🟡 🔴 ⚫`) or themed equivalents for user status; map these to presence data in Recoil.
- Provide affordances for creating channels/DMs (`+ Add Channel`, `+ New Message`).
- Collapse the sidebar on narrow widths; expose a toggle in responsive breakpoints.

## User Presence Panel
- List online users with real-time updates; include last seen text for offline users (e.g., `Last: 2h ago`).
- Clicking a user should open or focus the corresponding DM channel (create it if absent).
- Use avatars or initials; fall back to `Avatar` with user initials when photo missing.

## Composer Experience
- Input area accepts multi-line text; Enter sends, Shift+Enter inserts newline.
- Include emoji picker access, file attachment entry point, and optional sound toggle for notifications.
- Autosave drafts in `messagingDraftState` keyed by channel so switching channels preserves work.

## Notifications & Responsiveness
- Display desktop notifications/badge counts when tab inactive (respect user settings).
- Badge unread totals in both sidebar entries and browser title.
- Ensure layout adapts from desktop (three-column) to mobile (stacked view with collapsible sidebar and presence panel).
